---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import MailingList from "../../components/MailingList.astro";
---

<Layout>
        <div id="tour6" class="tour hidden">
                <h1>Contact!</h1>
                <br />
                <br />
                <p>
                        This page I spent very little time on cause truly, I
                        doubt anyone will be using it. I'm not notable enough to
                        have people want to contact me. One notable thing on
                        this page though is the sign up form to my newsletter.
                        It sends the responses to a site called forminnit which
                        then adds the responses to a list and emails me. I
                        thought that was pretty cool.
                </p>
                <button
                        class="tourBtn"
                        onclick="window.location.replace('achievements/?tour=5')"
                        >Back</button
                >
                <button
                        class="tourBtn"
                        onclick="window.location.replace('?tour=7')"
                        >The other stuff</button
                >
        </div>
        <div id="tour7" class="tour hidden">
                <h1>The other stuff</h1><br /><br />
                <p>
                        And now for all the other cool things on the site. Have
                        a look at the navbar! That shows up on every page thanks
                        to Astro! It's just a bunch of hyperlinks but without it
                        the site is pretty much useless. Notice how the contact
                        button looks different? That happens to the page your on
                        currently. It's a small change but I think it makes the
                        site feel completely different. It adds a responsive
                        feeling to the whole page I feel.
                </p>
                <button
                        class="tourBtn"
                        onclick="window.location.replace('?tour=6')"
                >
                        Contactino</button
                >
                <button
                        class="tourBtn"
                        onclick="window.location.replace('?tour=8')"
                >
                        More of the other stuff</button
                >
        </div>
        <div id="tour8" class="tour hidden">
                <h1>More nicheness</h1><br /><br />
                <p>
                        Look at the background, quite slick wouldn't you say? It
                        also took me like 2 minutes to implement and adjust to
                        my liking but it makes a huge difference to the site. It
                        removes the nothingness from the empty space and adds
                        texture. Infact I would say it helps people focus on the
                        text.<br />
                        <br />
                        But hey! That's all I got for you right now. I hope you emjoyed
                        the tour and the website. Thanks for the work you do, reviewer!
                </p>
                <button
                        class="tourBtn"
                        onclick="window.location.replace('?tour=7')"
                >
                        Back</button
                >

                <button
                        class="tourBtn"
                        onclick="window.location.replace('../')"
                >
                        Back Home!</button
                >
        </div>
        <h1><strong><em> Get in contact with me!</em></strong></h1><br /><br />
        <h3>Platforms I use:</h3>
        <a
                href="https://hackclub.slack.com/team/U09K59BPM2M"
                class="contactLink">Slack</a
        >
        <a href="mailto:jamesferris447@gmail.com" class="contactLink">E-mail</a>
        <p>uhh.. yeah, that's really the only two ways to message me rn</p><br
        /><br />
        <h3>Join my mailing list!</h3><br />
        <p>
                I send weekly emails about cool stuff happening in the tech
                world and promote stuff I belive in!
        </p>
        <MailingList />
</Layout>
<script>
        const params = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);

        if (params.get("tour") === "6") {
                document.getElementById("tour6")?.classList.remove("hidden");
        }

        if (params.get("tour") === "7") {
                document.getElementById("tour7")?.classList.remove("hidden");
        }

        if (params.get("tour") === "8") {
                document.getElementById("tour8")?.classList.remove("hidden");
        }
</script>
